bot:hasElement a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "té element"@ca,
        "má element"@cs,
        "har element"@da,
        "hat Bauteil"@de,
        "has element"@en,
        "alberga elemento"@es,
        "المان دارد"@fa,
        "omaa elementin"@fi,
        "a élément"@fr,
        "ha elemento"@it,
        "heeft element"@nl,
        "tem elemento"@pt,
        "má element"@sk,
        "värd för element"@sv,
        "Elemanı var"@tr,
        "含构件"@zh-cn ;
    rdfs:comment "Vincula una zona a un element que està contingut en, o és adjacent a, o interseca amb la zona. L'ús previst d'aquesta relació no s'ha d'establir explícitament, sinó inferir-se de les seves subpropietats. Permetrà, per exemple, consultar totes les portes d'un edifici donat que tenen una adjacència als espais de l'edifici."@ca,
        "Napojuje zónu na stavební prvek, který se buďto nachází v dané zóně, nebo je na její rozhraní. Využitelnost tohoto vztahu není daná explicitně, ale je vyvozená z vlastností zúčastněných prvků. Například to umožní vyhledat všechny dveře, které se dotýkají konkrétních zón."@cs,
        "Forbinder en Zone til en bygningsdel der enten er indeholdt i eller tilstødende til zonen. Det er ikke hensigten at denne relation angives eksplicit, men at den udledes af dennes underegneskaber. Det vil for eksempel tillade en forespørgsel på alle døre i en bygning givet at disse er enten tilstødende eller indeholdt i rum i bygningen."@da,
        "Beziehung zwischen einer Zone und einem Bauteil, dass entweder in der Zone enthalten ist, angrenzend ist, oder sich mit ihr schneidet. Diese Beziehung sollte nicht explizit benutzt werden, sondern ergibt sich implizit aus den Unterbeziehungen. Es ermöglicht, zum Beispiel, dass mit einer Abfrage alle Türen eines Gebäudes, die sich mit einer Zone schneiden ermittelt werden können."@de,
        "Links a Zone to an Element that is either contained in, adjacent to or intersecting with the Zone. The intended use of this relationship is not to be stated explicitly, but to be inferred from its sub-properties. It will, for example, allow one to query for all the doors of a building given that they have an adjacency to spaces of the building."@en,
        "Vincula una zona a un elemento que está contenido en, o es adyacente a, o interseca con la zona. El uso previsto de esta relación no es su definición explícita, sino inferirse de sus subpropiedades. Permitirá, por ejemplo, consultar todas las puertas de un edificio dado que tienen una adyacencia a los espacios del edificio."@es,
        "رابطه یک منطقه با المانی که یا توسط منطقه در برگرفته شده و یا همجوار است. کاربرد این رابطه نه لزوماً به صورت مستقیم که بلکه برای نتیجه‌گیری حاصل از زیر-روابط ابراز شده است.این رابطه، به عنوان مثال، امکان استعلام (query) از همه درهای یک ساختمان که در مجاورت فضای خاصی هستند را فراهم می کند."@fa,
        "Liittää vyöhykkeen (bot:Zone) elementtiin (bot:Element) joka on joko vyöhykkeen sisällä tai vierellä, tai leikkaa sen. Tätä suhdetta ei ole tarkoitus käyttää eksplisiittisesti, vaan se on pääteltävissä sen alaominaisuuksista. Mahdollistaa esimerkiksi kaikkien rakennuksen ovien hakemisen, kunhan ovet on merkitty rakennuksen tilojen viereisiksi elementeiksi (bot:adjacentElement)."@fi,
        "Relie une zone à un élément qui est soit contenu dans la zone, adjacent à celle-ci, ou intersectant. L'utilisation prévue de cette relation ne doit pas être indiquée explicitement, mais doit être déduite de ses sous-propriétés. Elle permettra, par exemple, d'interroger toutes les portes d'un bâtiment si elles sont adjacentes à certains des espaces du bâtiment."@fr,
        "Collega una zona ad un elemento che è contenuto, adiacente o intersecante la zona stessa. Non si prevede l'uso esplicito di questa relazione che deve essere inferita dalle sue sotto-proprietà. Per esempio, permette di cercare tutte le porte di un edificio dato che sono adiacenti agli spazi di un edificio."@it,
        "Verbindt een bot:Zone instantie met een bot:Element instantie die er ofwel door bevat wordt, aangrenzend aan is of snijdend mee is. Het is aangeraden om deze relatie niet expliciet te maken, maar af te leiden uit het gebruik van zijn sub relaties. Deze relatie maakt het bijvoorbeeld mogelijk om alle deuren van een gebouw op te vragen als die aangrenzend gedefinieerd zijn aan de ruimtes van het gebouw."@nl,
        "Relaciona uma zona com um elemento que está contido em, é adjacente ou intersecta a zona. Não se pretende que esta relação seja declarada explicitamente mas que seja inferida através das suas sub-propriedades. Esta propriedade permitirá, por exemplo, que se faça um query a todas as portas de um edifício que sejam adjacentes a espaços do edifício."@pt,
        "Napojuje zónu na stavebný prvok, ktorý sa buď nachádza v danej zóne alebo je na jej rozhraní. Využitie tohto vzťahu nie je definované explicitne, ale je vyvodené z vlastností zúčastnených prvkov. Napríklad to umožní vyhľadať všetky dvere v budove, ktoré sa dotýkajú nejakých zón."@sk,
        "Länkar en Zon till en Byggnadsdel som antingen inryms i eller ligger jämte zonen. Den här relationen är inte avseddd att uttryckas explicit, utan den kommer att härledas från under-relationer. Detta möjliggör till exempel att man kan fråga efter samtliga dörrar i en byggnad givet att de ligger i anslutning till utrymmen i byggnaden."@sv,
        "Bir Bölgeyi, Bölgenin içinde veya yanında bulunan bir bina parçasına bağlar. Bu ilişkinin açık bir şekilde ifade edilmesi değil, alt özellikleri türetilmesi amaçlanmaktadır. Örneğin, bunların binadaki odalara bitişik ya da bitişik olduğu göz önüne alındığında, bir binadaki tüm kapılar için bir sorgu'ya izin verecektir."@tr,
        "将区域链接到包含在区域中或附近的构件。 该关系的预期用途不是明确说明的，而是要从其子属性中推断出来。例如，如果构件与建筑物的空间相邻，可以借此查询建筑物的所有门。"@zh-cn ;
    rdfs:domain bot:Zone ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy bot: ;
    rdfs:range bot:Element ;
    owl:propertyChainAxiom ( bot:containsZone bot:hasElement ) ;
    vs:term_status "stable" .

ficr:Compromised a owl:Class,
        owl:NamedIndividual,
        ficr:AssessmentState,
        ficr:Compromised,
        ficr:ConditionState ;
    rdfs:label "Compromised"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "A condition state indicating that the physical performance of a boundary element is degraded or unreliable."@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ficr:ConditionState ;
    owl:disjointWith ficr:Effective,
        ficr:Unknown .

ficr:DeficiencyFinding a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "DeficiencyFinding"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "An inspection finding that records an observed defect, shortfall, obstruction, damage, missing evidence, or other adverse condition relevant to fire-related O&M assessment."@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ficr:InspectionFinding .

ficr:EvidenceMissing a owl:Class,
        owl:NamedIndividual,
        ficr:AssessmentState,
        ficr:EvidenceMissing,
        ficr:EvidenceStatus ;
    rdfs:label "EvidenceMissing"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "An evidence status indicating that no supporting evidence is available for the finding or record."@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ficr:EvidenceStatus ;
    owl:disjointWith ficr:EvidenceNotRequired .

ficr:EvidenceNotRequired a owl:Class,
        owl:NamedIndividual,
        ficr:AssessmentState,
        ficr:EvidenceNotRequired,
        ficr:EvidenceStatus ;
    rdfs:label "EvidenceNotRequired"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "An evidence status indicating that supporting evidence is not required for the finding or record."@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ficr:EvidenceStatus .

ficr:ExternalWallDoor a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "ExternalWallDoor"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "An external wall door is a door that is part of a building's exterior wall, providing an entrance and exit to the building."@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ficr:Doorset ;
    owl:equivalentClass [ a owl:Class ;
            owl:intersectionOf ( ficr:Doorset [ a owl:Restriction ;
                        owl:hasValue true ;
                        owl:onProperty ficr:isExternal ] ) ] .

ficr:Gallery a owl:Class,
        owl:NamedIndividual,
        ficr:Gallery,
        ficr:SpaceUsage,
        ficr:UsageType ;
    rdfs:label "Gallery"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "A floor or balcony that does not extend across the full extent of a building’s footprint and is open to the floor below."@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ficr:SpaceUsage ;
    owl:disjointWith ficr:HabitableRoom,
        ficr:Kitchen,
        ficr:PlaceOfSpecialHazard,
        ficr:ServiceUsage,
        ficr:Warehouse .

ficr:GroundAndAboveStorey a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "GroundAndAboveStorey"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "A storey at or above ground level, defined by isAboveGround = true."@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf bot:Storey ;
    owl:equivalentClass [ a owl:Class ;
            owl:intersectionOf ( bot:Storey [ a owl:Restriction ;
                        owl:hasValue true ;
                        owl:onProperty ficr:isAboveGround ] ) ] .

ficr:Hall a owl:Class,
        owl:NamedIndividual,
        ficr:CirculationUsage,
        ficr:Hall,
        ficr:SpaceUsage,
        ficr:UsageType ;
    rdfs:label "Hall"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "A \"hall\" in a building can refer to a large, central room or a long, narrow passageway."@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ficr:CirculationUsage ;
    owl:disjointWith ficr:Lobby .

ficr:LiftSystem a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "LiftSystem"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Complete machinery and infrastructure for vertical transport."@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ficr:VerticalTransportSystem .

ficr:ProtectedStairwaySpace a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "ProtectedStairwaySpace"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "A stairway space that leads to a final exit to a place of safety and that is adequately enclosed with fire resisting construction. Included in the definition is any exit passageway between the foot of the stair and the final exit."@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ficr:FireProtectionSpatialProvision ;
    owl:equivalentClass [ a owl:Class ;
            owl:intersectionOf ( bot:Zone [ a owl:Restriction ;
                        owl:onProperty bot:containsElement ;
                        owl:someValuesFrom ficr:Stair ] [ a owl:Restriction ;
                        owl:onProperty ficr:hasZoneFireSafetyRole ;
                        owl:someValuesFrom ficr:PassiveFireProtectionRole ] ) ] .

ficr:PurposeGroup2 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "PurposeGroup2"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Residential other than Dwellings."@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ficr:PurposeGroup .

ficr:PurposeGroup7 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "PurposeGroup7"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Storage and Car Parking"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ficr:PurposeGroup .

ficr:Railing a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Railing"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "A railing refers to a protective barrier or fence, usually made of metal (such as wrought or cast iron, steel, or aluminium), timber, or plastic, designed to provide safety and support."@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ficr:FabricElement .

ficr:RoofSpace a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "RoofSpace"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "A roof space is the area inside a building between the ceiling of the top floor and the underside of the roof."@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf bot:Space ;
    owl:disjointWith ficr:RoomSpace,
        ficr:ShaftSpace,
        ficr:StairSpace .

ficr:SwitchGearRoom a owl:Class,
        owl:NamedIndividual,
        ficr:PlaceOfSpecialHazard,
        ficr:SpaceUsage,
        ficr:SwitchGearRoom,
        ficr:UsageType ;
    rdfs:label "SwitchGearRoom"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "A switchgear room in a building is a dedicated space that houses electrical equipment used to control, protect, and isolate the building's electrical system, such as circuit breakers, switches, and fuses."@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ficr:PlaceOfSpecialHazard ;
    owl:disjointWith ficr:TransformerRoom .

ficr:UndeterminedResult a owl:Class,
        owl:NamedIndividual,
        ficr:AssessmentState,
        ficr:ComplianceResult,
        ficr:UndeterminedResult ;
    rdfs:label "UndeterminedResult"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "A compliance result indicating that the compliance status could not be determined from available evidence."@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ficr:ComplianceResult .

ficr:hasSystemFireSafetyRole a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "hasSystemFireSafetyRole"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Assigns a fire safety role to a building system, such as active protection, protected supply, evacuation support, or firefighting support."@en ;
    rdfs:domain ficr:BuildingSystem ;
    rdfs:range ficr:FireSafetyRole ;
    rdfs:subPropertyOf ficr:hasFireSafetyRole ;
    owl:inverseOf ficr:isSystemFireSafetyRoleOf .

ficr:isFireSafetyRoleOf a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "isFireSafetyRoleOf"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Inverse of hasFireSafetyRole."@en ;
    rdfs:subPropertyOf ficr:isUsageTypeOf .

ficr:isUsageTypeOf a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "isUsageTypeOf"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Inverse of hasUsageType."@en .

